---
import PrepLayout from '../../../layouts/PrepLayout.astro';
import { FRONTIER_LABS } from '../../../data/frontierLabs';
import { SITE } from '../../../consts';
if (!SITE.features.prepTools) return Astro.redirect('/questions/', 302);
---

<PrepLayout
  title="Executable frontier ML interview labs"
  description="Original, runnable work samples for agentic coding, LLM training debugging, model investigation, inference, performance, post-training, implementation, and math."
  heading="Practice the work sample, not just the answer."
  lede="Current senior ML and Research Engineer loops increasingly use codebases, traces, notebooks, presentations, and open-ended investigations. These labs turn those formats into bounded, executable practice without publishing leaked questions."
>
  <section class="callout"><h2>Use only confirmed formats</h2><p>Do not complete every lab. Ask the recruiter for the assessment type, duration, editor, AI policy, expected artifact, and review format. Then choose the closest exercise and keep the rest optional.</p></section>

  <div class="lab-grid">
    {FRONTIER_LABS.map((lab) => (
      <a class="lab-card" href={`/prep/labs/${lab.slug}/`}>
        <p>{lab.eyebrow}</p>
        <h2>{lab.title}</h2>
        <span>{lab.duration}</span>
        <small>{lab.description}</small>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Rules shared by every lab</h2>
  <ol class="step-list">
    <li><strong>Start from the contract.</strong> State inputs, outputs, invariants, timebox, and forbidden shortcuts before touching code.</li>
    <li><strong>Preserve evidence.</strong> Keep failing tests, traces, probe results, and rejected hypotheses. A clean final state hides how you reasoned.</li>
    <li><strong>Use AI only when allowed.</strong> Some labs intentionally support an agent. Others model closed-book or no-AI rounds.</li>
    <li><strong>Review before accepting.</strong> Generated code, grader outputs, and model explanations are untrusted until you verify them.</li>
    <li><strong>Finish with a decision.</strong> State what works, what remains uncertain, and the next highest-information action.</li>
  </ol>

  <section class="callout"><h2>Not a question dump</h2><p>The labs are original exercises derived from public format evidence and current role demands. They do not reproduce confidential prompts, and they should not be presented as exact company questions.</p><p><a href="/prep/frontier-labs/">Check current process evidence →</a></p></section>
</PrepLayout>

<style>
  .lab-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .9rem; }
  .lab-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--c-rule); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .lab-card:hover { border-color: var(--c-accent); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .lab-card p { margin: 0 0 .35rem; color: var(--c-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .66rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lab-card h2 { margin: 0 0 .35rem !important; font-size: 1.05rem !important; }
  .lab-card span { color: var(--c-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .72rem; }
  .lab-card small { margin-top: .65rem; color: var(--c-text-soft); font-size: .82rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .lab-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
